Q: Expecting specific error when writing unit tests in jest
A: <p>Compared to examples in <a href="https://jestjs.io/docs/en/tutorial-async" rel="noreferrer">jest documentation</a>, you may have 2 problems here.</p>
<ul>
<li><code>await</code> should be outside the <code>expect</code> argument</li>
<li><code>rejects</code> implies an error was thrown, so you test for equality</li>
</ul>
<p>Something like:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>it('test', async () =&gt; {
